        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Right, right.\n\nWell, I used it all the time in vim – especially in LaTeX. I just don't quite see how me using `gcc` on an empty line not doing anything is more useful than it doing something … but, yeah, I see that it's reasonable to model the built-in behavior. It also seems more consistent to me that the `ignore_blank_lines` option would apply regardless of the presence of non-blank lines – though I see that this can't be changed, given the origin of the behavior, and its established/documented status.\n\nSome way of configuring whether one wants the built-in behavior or a consistent treatment of blank lines would be great, I guess … but I fully understand if that's not something you're interested in.",
