            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Some way of configuring whether one wants the built-in behavior or a consistent treatment of blank lines would be great, I guess … but I fully understand if that's not something you're interested in.\n\nThe main point is that current behavior *is* consistent treatment, as was already described in [this comment](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/issues/22#issuecomment-3018659494).\n\n> I just don't quite see how me using `gcc` on an empty line not doing anything is more useful than it doing something …\n\nIt is more consistent with how an action is decided. Describing it as \"uncomment if every line is comment or blank but not if all lines are blank, comment otherwise\" is more confusing than the current behavior.\n\nAside from theoretical issues, there is also a practical one about deciding the indent of the added comment block. The indent is something computed as \"whitespace from line start to first non-blank character\", which requires a non-blank character. Treating the whole line as indent and adding comment leaders at the end of the widest blank line is something I don't really like to have.",
            "created_at": "2025-06-30T11:10:15Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/22#issuecomment-3018744272",
